        <mxCell id="7e5ppZ3mdL3I-DvPp26F-13" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" value="Outputs:&lt;br&gt;T-test (p&amp;lt;0.05) and KS test gif visualisations" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="170" x="530" y="655" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="JFY1F2Ew3XQokm6CrdP7-13" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of the two skull analysis pipelines.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;(A) In the single-subject branch, a head image is processed to generate an aligned surface mesh, which is compared against the reference distribution to compute per-face Mahalanobis distances; results are visualised as per-subject Mahalanobis GIFs.&lt;br&gt;(B) In the cohort branch, multiple subjects are processed to aligned meshes and analysed collectively to compute cohort-level per-face statistical differences (t-test and Kolmogorov–Smirnov test), visualised as significance GIFs.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="560" x="50" y="760" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
